From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Batman <batman@Batman.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:24:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] browse patch 011: noise canvas getImageData readback per
 origin
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

getImageData() is one of the two classic canvas-fingerprinting
readouts: draw a deterministic scene, read pixels back, hash them.
Because rendering is bit-identical across machines sharing a
GPU/font stack, that hash is a stable cross-site tracking id.

Perturb ~1 in 8 pixels by +-1 on one RGB channel (never alpha), keyed
by a per-process random salt XORed with a hash of the calling
origin. Same origin -> same pattern for the life of the process
(repeated getImageData calls from one page stay internally
consistent, and the pattern can't be voted out by reading twice).
Different origins -> unrelated patterns, so the noise itself cannot
become a new cross-site correlation signal. Browser restart -> new
salt -> every site's pattern changes, so it cannot become a
long-lived id either.

Shared BaseRenderingContext2D::getImageDataInternal() covers both
<canvas> and OffscreenCanvas 2D contexts from one call site.
toDataURL()/toBlob() go through a separate encode path (Snapshot(),
not getImageData) and are deliberately a follow-up patch (012) — a
different file/function deserves its own verification pass rather
than riding along here. Audio fingerprinting (WebAudio) is patch 013
for the same reason.
